  "status": "PROVED CERTIFIER REDUCTION: PARITY-MATCHED INTERVAL QUOTIENTS STRIP X+1 SAFELY",
  "task": "X72 h=4 interval X+1 strip",
  "theorem": "For q=1+eps*(X^a+...+X^(a+ell-1)), q(-1)=0 if and only if ell is odd and eps*(-1)^a=-1.  In that case q=(X+1)h.  For 2-power n>=4, Phi_n(-1)=2, so odd row characteristic makes p | Res(Phi_n,q) equivalent to p | Res(Phi_n,h).  The strip flag is invariant on X68 certifier keys because it is equivalent to the original four-term word vanishing at -1, and the X64/Galois key operations preserve that vanishing."
}
